{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"746","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. New Roads"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cities in Berland, each of them has a unique id — an integer from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", the capital is the one with id "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". Now there is a serious problem in Berland with roads — there are no roads."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"That is why there was a decision to build "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" roads so that there will be exactly one simple path between each pair of cities."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the construction plan "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., at"},{"kind":"text","text":" were stated, where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals to the distance from the capital to the most distant city, concerning new roads. "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals the number of cities which should be at the distance "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the capital. The distance between two cities is the number of roads one has to pass on the way from one city to another. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Also, it was decided that among all the cities except the capital there should be exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" cities with exactly one road going from each of them. Such cities are dead-ends and can't be economically attractive. In calculation of these cities the capital is not taken into consideration regardless of the number of roads from it. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to offer a plan of road's construction which satisfies all the described conditions or to inform that it is impossible."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains three positive numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 2·105"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ t, k < n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the distance to the most distant city from the capital and the number of cities which should be dead-ends (the capital in this number is not taken into consideration). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a sequence of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., at"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai < n"},{"kind":"text","text":"), the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th number is the number of cities which should be at the distance "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the capital. It is guaranteed that the sum of all the values "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is impossible to built roads which satisfy all conditions, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Otherwise, in the first line print one integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of cities in Berland. In the each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" line print two integers — the ids of cities that are connected by a road. Each road should be printed exactly once. You can print the roads and the cities connected by a road in any order."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple answers, print any of them. Remember that the capital has id "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7 3 3\n2 3 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7\n1 3\n2 1\n2 6\n2 4\n7 4\n3 5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"14 5 6\n4 4 2 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"14\n3 1\n1 4\n11 6\n1 2\n10 13\n6 10\n10 12\n14 12\n8 4\n5 1\n3 7\n2 6\n5 9\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 1 1\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"G","problemCode":"746G","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/746/problem/G"}